  "id": "EDU009",
  "title": "The Mirror-Tile Repair",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "basic math",
  "premise": "A mosaic maker must repair a reflected pattern, but copies a tile to the same side of the mirror line. Folding the drawing makes paired positions touch and reveals the missing tile location.",
  "hook": "Where would this tile land if the page folded?",
  "visible_action": "A dashed axis becomes a hinge; square tiles reflect across it along perpendicular guide tracks.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Reflection preserves distance to the mirror line on the opposite side.",
  "gate": "Use an explicit reflection axis and avoid confusing reflection with rotation.",
